/A 941 0 R
/Alt (Wiring diagram for the experimental setup. Voltage, Current, Distal Tach, and Motor Tach BNC go from the experimental setup interface box to the cDAQ chassis BNC analog breakout board Mod 1. These are input into AI0, AI1, AI2, and AI3 respectively. Voltage and Distal Tach are also connected by BNC T-connectors to CH1 and CH2 of the oscilloscope respectively. The motor affixed to the setup is powered by the Techron Power Supply Amplifier; CH1 Out Red on the amplifier is connected to +VDC on the setup, and CH1 Out Black on the amplifier is connected to COM on the setup. The amplifier is connected by BNC cable to the Keysight Waveform Generator; CH1 In on the amplifier is connected to the front Output terminal on the waveform generator. When using the Random Noise, Trapezoid, or CSV File tabs, CH1 In on the amplifier is instead connected to AO1 on the BNC analog breakout board. The waveform generator when utilized is connected via USB cable to the workstation PC. )
/K [1]
/P 39 0 R
/Pg 38 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
